                <pb facs="0578" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.74/196: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-11-14T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 14,
                                1921—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 14—4:35
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>396. An official in the Ministry of Communications and a representative of Moss
                    inform me that the recent default of the Chinese Government may render it
                    impossible to secure funds for the Federal wireless contract. American prestige
                    would be gravely injured should this contract fail to be financed as it is a
                    sound business project unconnected with the solvency of the Chinese Government.
                    The Department’s good offices to ensure success are urgently requested.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
